{"id": "section-body-16492", "title": "Recurrent Respiratory Papillomatosis (Laryngeal Papillomas)", "chapterId": "chapter-fifteen", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "EAR, NOSE AND THROAT/HEAD AND NECK DISEASES", "Throat Conditions", "Recurrent Respiratory Papillomatosis (Laryngeal Papillomas)"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-16492", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Recurrent Respiratory Papillomatosis (Laryngeal Papillomas)", "runs": [{"text": "Recurrent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Respiratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Papillomatosis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(Laryngeal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Papillomas)"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1219"}}, {"id": "body-16493", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "It is the commonest benign laryngeal tumor of the larynx caused by Human papilloma virus (HPV), occurring in both children and adults. It has a higher recurrence rate in children than in adults, among adults it may turn into a malignancy.", "runs": [{"text": "It is the commonest benign laryngeal tumor of the larynx caused by Human papilloma virus (HPV), occurring in both children and adults. It has a higher recurrence rate in children than in adults, among adults it may turn into a malignancy."}]}, {"id": "body-16495", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-16496", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Hoarse voice, audible respiration (inspiratory stridor)", "runs": [{"text": "Hoarse"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "voice,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "audible"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "respiration"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(inspiratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stridor)"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1169"}}, {"id": "body-16497", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Progressive difficulty in breathing", "runs": [{"text": "Progressive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "difficulty"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "breathing"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1169"}}, {"id": "body-16498", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Progressive inspiratory stridor", "runs": [{"text": "Progressive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inspiratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "stridor"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1169"}}, {"id": "body-16499", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "On and off cough", "runs": [{"text": "On"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "off"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cough"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1169"}}, {"id": "body-16501", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Perform a thorough respiratory system examination", "runs": [{"text": "Perform"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "thorough"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "respiratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "system"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "examination"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1169"}}, {"id": "body-16502", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Indirect laryngoscopy for papilloma croups on the larynx", "runs": [{"text": "Indirect"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "laryngoscopy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "papilloma"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "croups"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "larynx"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1169"}}, {"id": "body-16503", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Rigid laryngoscopy (Endoscopy) OR Fiber optic Nasolaryngoscopy", "runs": [{"text": "Rigid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "laryngoscopy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(Endoscopy)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "OR"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Fiber"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "optic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Nasolaryngoscopy"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1169"}}, {"id": "body-16505", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Non-Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Non-Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-16506", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "If in distress, perform a tracheostomy first then refer", "runs": [{"text": "If"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "distress,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "perform"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tracheostomy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "first"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "then"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "refer"}]}, {"id": "body-16508", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Referral: Refer the patient to the next facility with adequate expertise and facilities", "runs": [{"text": "Referral:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Refer"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "next"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "facility"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "adequate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "expertise"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "facilities"}]}, {"id": "body-16510", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Surgical treatment", "runs": [{"text": "Surgical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "treatment"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-16511", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Microsurgical debridement is the mainstay, observe laryngeal mucosa and think of voice quality, avoid introducing anterior laryngeal web (Direct Laryngoscopy under GA+ microlaryngeal surgery(D/Scopy+MLS) Bronchoscopy is advised every time when doing Direct Laryngoscopy under GA", "runs": [{"text": "Microsurgical debridement is the mainstay, observe laryngeal mucosa and think of voice quality, avoid introducing anterior laryngeal web (Direct Laryngoscopy under GA+ microlaryngeal surgery(D/Scopy+MLS) Bronchoscopy is advised every time when doing Direct Laryngoscopy under GA"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1169"}}, {"id": "body-16512", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Tracheostomy shall be avoided, if it has to be done, only short term", "runs": [{"text": "Tracheostomy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "shall"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "avoided,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "if"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "it"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "has"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "done,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "only"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "short"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "term"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1169"}}], "source": {"file": "medical.docx", "chapter": "Ear, nose and throat/head and neck diseases", "start": "body-16492", "end": "body-16512"}}